IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`
IMPORT `P1-art-6`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-art-9.l4 -- ARTICLE 9: PROCESSING OF SPECIAL CATEGORIES OF PERSONAL DATA.  Layer 1 (P1).
-- Art 9(1) prohibits; Art 9(2) says "Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies"; (3) and (4)
-- qualify.  LIFTING THE PROHIBITION IS NOT LAWFULNESS: Art 6 still has to be met (the text of Art 9 says only
-- that paragraph 1 does not apply).  The functions answer questions about the prohibition, never "may I".
-- Whose duty: Art 9(1) names no party; it is encoded as a prohibition addressed to the CONTROLLER (assumed,
-- not ruled: Art 5(2), Art 24(1) and Art 4(7) make the controller responsible for the processing; fork F9-1).
-- Who may rely on it: the data subject.
-- Borrowed facts (plain inputs, PLAN.md section 4): the data kinds of Art 4(13)-(15) (genetic, biometric, health:
-- K2) arrive as a choice in `Art 9(1) category of personal data`; "consent" (Art 4(11)); "explicit" is a judgment;
-- Art 89(1) safeguards (P9).
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 9(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 9(1) process personal data of a category named in paragraph 1`

§ `Article 9(1): the categories and the prohibition`

-- src:121 | 1. Processing of personal data revealing racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, or trade union membership, and the processing of genetic data, biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person, data concerning health or data concerning a natural person's sex life or sexual orientation shall be prohibited.
@ref Art 9(1): the categories (src:121)
GIVEN `the categories of personal data processed` IS A LIST OF `Art 9(1) category of personal data`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(1) the categories processed include one that paragraph 1 names` MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD NOT (    c EQUALS `Art 9(1) biometric data not for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person`
                            OR c EQUALS `Art 9(1) other personal data`))
        `the categories of personal data processed`
    -- a membership test on the facts, not a decision of the text; the two members outside the list are biometric data NOT used "for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person" and every other personal data

§ `Article 9(2): the ten grounds`

-- src:122 | 2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies:
-- src:123 | (a) the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing of those personal data for one or more specified purposes, except where Union or Member State law provide that the prohibition referred to in paragraph 1 may not be lifted by the data subject;
@ref Art 9(2)(a) (src:122-123)
GIVEN `the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing of those personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent is for one or more specified purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Union or Member State law provides that the prohibition referred to in paragraph 1 may not be lifted by the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(2)(a) point (a) applies: the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing for one or more specified purposes` MEANS
    IF `the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing of those personal data`
       AND `the consent is for one or more specified purposes`
       AND NOT (`Union or Member State law provides that the prohibition referred to in paragraph 1 may not be lifted by the data subject`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "except where"): "except where Union or Member State law provide that the prohibition referred to in paragraph 1 may not be lifted by the data subject"; and a failed "if" of point (a) (marginal reading (a), NOTES.md)

-- src:122 | 2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies:
-- src:124 | (b) processing is necessary for the purposes of carrying out the obligations and exercising specific rights of the controller or of the data subject in the field of employment and social security and social protection law in so far as it is authorised by Union or Member State law or a collective agreement pursuant to Member State law providing for appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject;
@ref Art 9(2)(b) (src:122-124)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for carrying out the obligations and exercising specific rights of the controller or of the data subject in the field of employment and social security and social protection law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is authorised by Union or Member State law or a collective agreement pursuant to Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that law or agreement provides for appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(2)(b) point (b) applies: the processing is necessary for employment and social security and social protection law` MEANS
    IF `the processing is necessary for carrying out the obligations and exercising specific rights of the controller or of the data subject in the field of employment and social security and social protection law`
       AND `it is authorised by Union or Member State law or a collective agreement pursuant to Member State law`
       AND `that law or agreement provides for appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "if", "in so far as"): "in so far as it is authorised by Union or Member State law or a collective agreement pursuant to Member State law providing for appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject"

-- src:122 | 2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies:
-- src:125 | (c) processing is necessary to protect the vital interests of the data subject or of another natural person where the data subject is physically or legally incapable of giving consent;
@ref Art 9(2)(c) (src:122-125)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary to protect vital interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `whose vital interests` IS AN `Art 6(1)(d) whose vital interests`
      `the data subject is physically or legally incapable of giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(2)(c) point (c) applies: the processing is necessary to protect vital interests where the data subject cannot give consent` MEANS
    IF `the processing is necessary to protect vital interests`
       AND NOT (`whose vital interests` EQUALS `Art 6(1)(d) the interests of something that is not a natural person`)
       AND `the data subject is physically or legally incapable of giving consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "if", "where"): "processing is necessary to protect the vital interests of the data subject or of another natural person where the data subject is physically or legally incapable of giving consent"

DECLARE `Art 9(2)(d) kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `Art 9(2)(d) a foundation`
    `Art 9(2)(d) an association`
    `Art 9(2)(d) another not-for-profit body`
    `Art 9(2)(d) a body that is not a not-for-profit body`

DECLARE `Art 9(2)(d) aim of the body` IS ONE OF
    `Art 9(2)(d) a political aim`
    `Art 9(2)(d) a philosophical aim`
    `Art 9(2)(d) a religious aim`
    `Art 9(2)(d) a trade union aim`
    `Art 9(2)(d) some other aim`

-- src:122 | 2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies:
-- src:126 | (d) processing is carried out in the course of its legitimate activities with appropriate safeguards by a foundation, association or any other not-for-profit body with a political, philosophical, religious or trade union aim and on condition that the processing relates solely to the members or to former members of the body or to persons who have regular contact with it in connection with its purposes and that the personal data are not disclosed outside that body without the consent of the data subjects;
@ref Art 9(2)(d) (src:122-126)
GIVEN `the processing is carried out in the course of its legitimate activities with appropriate safeguards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is` IS AN `Art 9(2)(d) kind of body`
      `the body has` IS AN `Art 9(2)(d) aim of the body`
      `the processing relates solely to the members or to former members of the body or to persons who have regular contact with it in connection with its purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are disclosed outside that body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subjects have consented to that disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(2)(d) point (d) applies: a foundation, association or other not-for-profit body processes data of its members and those in regular contact with it` MEANS
    IF `the processing is carried out in the course of its legitimate activities with appropriate safeguards`
       AND NOT (`the body is` EQUALS `Art 9(2)(d) a body that is not a not-for-profit body`)
       AND NOT (`the body has` EQUALS `Art 9(2)(d) some other aim`)
       AND `the processing relates solely to the members or to former members of the body or to persons who have regular contact with it in connection with its purposes`
       AND ((NOT (`the personal data are disclosed outside that body`)) OR `the data subjects have consented to that disclosure`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a failed "if", marginal reading (a)): "Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies"; point (d) is within it only "on condition that the processing relates solely to the members or to former members of the body or to persons who have regular contact with it in connection with its purposes and that the personal data are not disclosed outside that body without the consent of the data subjects"

-- src:122 | 2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies:
