    `Art 9(2)(h) Member State law`
    `Art 9(2)(h) a contract with a health professional`
    `Art 9(2)(h) none of these`

-- src:122 | 2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies:
-- src:130 | (h) processing is necessary for the purposes of preventive or occupational medicine, for the assessment of the working capacity of the employee, medical diagnosis, the provision of health or social care or treatment or the management of health or social care systems and services on the basis of Union or Member State law or pursuant to contract with a health professional and subject to the conditions and safeguards referred to in paragraph 3;
@ref Art 9(2)(h) (src:122-130)
GIVEN `the purpose of the processing` IS AN `Art 9(2)(h) purpose`
      `the processing is necessary for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is on the basis of` IS AN `Art 9(2)(h) basis`
      `the conditions and safeguards referred to in paragraph 3 are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(2)(h) point (h) applies: the processing is necessary for preventive or occupational medicine, health or social care or treatment, or the management of health or social care systems` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the purpose of the processing` EQUALS `Art 9(2)(h) some other purpose`)
       AND `the processing is necessary for that purpose`
       AND NOT (`the processing is on the basis of` EQUALS `Art 9(2)(h) none of these`)
       AND `the conditions and safeguards referred to in paragraph 3 are met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a failed "if", marginal reading (a)): "processing is necessary for the purposes of preventive or occupational medicine, for the assessment of the working capacity of the employee, medical diagnosis, the provision of health or social care or treatment or the management of health or social care systems and services on the basis of Union or Member State law or pursuant to contract with a health professional and subject to the conditions and safeguards referred to in paragraph 3"

DECLARE `Art 9(2)(i) reason` IS ONE OF
    `Art 9(2)(i) protecting against serious cross-border threats to health`
    `Art 9(2)(i) ensuring high standards of quality and safety of health care and of medicinal products or medical devices`
    `Art 9(2)(i) another reason of public interest in the area of public health`
    `Art 9(2)(i) no reason of public interest in the area of public health`

-- src:122 | 2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies:
-- src:131 | (i) processing is necessary for reasons of public interest in the area of public health, such as protecting against serious cross-border threats to health or ensuring high standards of quality and safety of health care and of medicinal products or medical devices, on the basis of Union or Member State law which provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject, in particular professional secrecy;
@ref Art 9(2)(i) (src:122-131)
GIVEN `the reason` IS AN `Art 9(2)(i) reason`
      `the processing is necessary for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is on the basis of Union or Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that law provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(2)(i) point (i) applies: the processing is necessary for reasons of public interest in the area of public health on the basis of law with suitable measures` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the reason` EQUALS `Art 9(2)(i) no reason of public interest in the area of public health`)
       AND `the processing is necessary for that reason`
       AND `it is on the basis of Union or Member State law`
       AND `that law provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a failed "if", marginal reading (a)): "processing is necessary for reasons of public interest in the area of public health, such as ... on the basis of Union or Member State law which provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject, in particular professional secrecy"
    -- "such as": the two reasons named are examples; any other reason of public interest in the area of public health also counts ("includes", so no reason outside the list is excluded). "in particular professional secrecy" names one such measure and is not a separate condition.

-- src:122 | 2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies:
