      `point (j)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(2) one of points (a) to (j) applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN x YIELD x EQUALS JUST TRUE)
               (LIST `point (a)`, `point (b)`, `point (c)`, `point (d)`, `point (e)`, `point (f)`, `point (g)`, `point (h)`, `point (i)`, `point (j)`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF all (GIVEN x YIELD x EQUALS JUST FALSE)
               (LIST `point (a)`, `point (b)`, `point (c)`, `point (d)`, `point (e)`, `point (f)`, `point (g)`, `point (h)`, `point (i)`, `point (j)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a failed "if", marginal reading (a)): "Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no point applies yet at least one point's answer is not covered

§ `Article 9(1) and (2): is the processing prohibited`

-- src:121 | 1. Processing of personal data revealing racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, or trade union membership, and the processing of genetic data, biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person, data concerning health or data concerning a natural person's sex life or sexual orientation shall be prohibited.
-- src:122 | 2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies:
@ref Art 9(1) and (2) (src:121-122)
GIVEN `the categories of personal data processed` IS A LIST OF `Art 9(1) category of personal data`
      `the answer of Art 9(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(1) the processing of personal data of a category named in paragraph 1 is prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 9(1) the categories processed include one that paragraph 1 names` `the categories of personal data processed`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is of "personal data revealing racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, or trade union membership", genetic data, "biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person", data concerning health and data concerning sex life or sexual orientation; for other data Art 9 is silent
        IF `the answer of Art 9(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative): "Paragraph 1 shall not apply if one of the following applies"
        IF `the answer of Art 9(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- "shall be prohibited": no point of paragraph 2 applies, so paragraph 1 stands
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether a point of paragraph 2 applies is not covered, so the text does not say whether the prohibition stands

-- The prohibition as a regulative rule.  Art 9(1) names no party; the controller is assumed (fork F9-1).  A SHANT has a breach
-- path: doing the act is the breach, with no deadline needed.
-- src:121 | 1. Processing of personal data revealing racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, or trade union membership, and the processing of genetic data, biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person, data concerning health or data concerning a natural person's sex life or sexual orientation shall be prohibited.
@ref Art 9(1), regulative form (src:121-121)
GIVEN `the prohibition applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 9(1) action`
`Art 9(1) the controller shall not process personal data of a category named in paragraph 1` MEANS
    IF `the prohibition applies`
    THEN PARTY `controller`
         SHANT `Art 9(1) process personal data of a category named in paragraph 1`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `controller` BECAUSE "the controller processed personal data of a category named in Art 9(1) while the prohibition applied"
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `Art 9(1) the controller shall not process personal data of a category named in paragraph 1` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `controller` DOES `Art 9(1) process personal data of a category named in paragraph 1` AT 5
-- Result on the main build: DEONTIC BREACHED.
#TRACE `Art 9(1) the controller shall not process personal data of a category named in paragraph 1` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- Result on the main build: the prohibition is still standing and unbroken.
#TRACE `Art 9(1) the controller shall not process personal data of a category named in paragraph 1` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `controller` DOES `Art 9(1) process personal data of a category named in paragraph 1` AT 5
-- Result on the main build: FULFILLED (a point of paragraph 2 applies, so paragraph 1 does not).

§ `Article 9(3) and (4)`

-- src:133 | 3. Personal data referred to in paragraph 1 may be processed for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2 when those data are processed by or under the responsibility of a professional subject to the obligation of professional secrecy under Union or Member State law or rules established by national competent bodies or by another person also subject to an obligation of secrecy under Union or Member State law or rules established by national competent bodies.
@ref Art 9(3) (src:133)
GIVEN `the processing is for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data are processed by or under the responsibility of a professional subject to the obligation of professional secrecy under Union or Member State law or rules established by national competent bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data are processed by another person also subject to an obligation of secrecy under Union or Member State law or rules established by national competent bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(3) personal data referred to in paragraph 1 may be processed for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the processing is for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2"
        IF `the data are processed by or under the responsibility of a professional subject to the obligation of professional secrecy under Union or Member State law or rules established by national competent bodies`
           OR `the data are processed by another person also subject to an obligation of secrecy under Union or Member State law or rules established by national competent bodies`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "when", split site (ii)): "when those data are processed by or under the responsibility of a professional subject to the obligation of professional secrecy ... or by another person also subject to an obligation of secrecy"; point (h) is itself "subject to the conditions and safeguards referred to in paragraph 3"

-- src:134 | 4. Member States may maintain or introduce further conditions, including limitations, with regard to the processing of genetic data, biometric data or data concerning health.
@ref Art 9(4) (src:134)
GIVEN `the category of the personal data` IS AN `Art 9(1) category of personal data`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(4) Member States may maintain or introduce further conditions, including limitations, with regard to the processing of genetic data, biometric data or data concerning health` MEANS
    IF `the category of the personal data` EQUALS `Art 9(1) genetic data`
       OR `the category of the personal data` EQUALS `Art 9(1) biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person`
       OR `the category of the personal data` EQUALS `Art 9(1) biometric data not for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person`
       OR `the category of the personal data` EQUALS `Art 9(1) data concerning health`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "with regard to the processing of genetic data, biometric data or data concerning health"; for the other categories the text does not say
